## English RFQ draft

**Subject: Technical RFQ / NDA request — fixed-material 79.75 mm sliding inter-chamber flex (8.2 mm seating), static BM28 endpoints & 7-inch rollable OLED**

We are evaluating an **unreleased research concept**, not an authorized production modification of any existing Motorola product. Two independently functional equal-outline compartments; the B compartment slides 79.75 mm and seats 8.2 mm normally; one ~7-inch flexible main OLED, no separate rear display; 300,000 target actuation cycles. The present CAD is **NOT qualified for manufacturing**.

Please confirm your official engineering/FAE route and NDA requirements before exchanging proprietary data. We request your exact released part/revision, original CAD plus neutral STEP and full keep-out volumes, mounting/PCB details and mating cycle ratings, signed A/B assembly interface/datum set with >=4 corresponding non-coplanar points and both tolerance limits, and explicit scope of permitted changes. For the flex/display route please provide actual copper stackup, neutral axis, dynamic bending radius, torsional limits, full-stroke fixed-material-coordinate service-loop shapes, strain relief and 300k-cycle raw electrical/physical fatigue measurements with sample counts and failure criteria. For electrical endpoints, additionally specify two-battery isolation/fault-injection and full-stroke USB signal integrity methods and unprocessed measurements. Include official provenance and SHA256 of each original artifact, signing-key fingerprint independently verifiable through your own published channel, and export/licensing restrictions. A public model download or self-signed attachment alone will not count as a controlled OEM approval.

Please reply with contact, NDA route and availability of evidence; **do not interpret this as a purchase order**.

